That paragraph is standard, and here is what it means in this particular case,
because the software does something specific and dangerous.

**This software deletes objects from snapshot repositories.** Oracle's Amazon
S3 Compatibility API exposes no object versioning, so a delete made through it
has no undo. The safety properties documented in this repository are real and
tested, and they are not a guarantee about your data, your repository or your
cluster.

Read `docs/quickstart-read-only.md` before you delete anything. The audit is
read-only and cannot delete; that is enforced structurally, not by convention.
Start there, keep the manifest, and satisfy yourself the answer is right before
acting on it.
